VEX IQ Prosthetic Knee Brace Demonstration

This video demonstrates my VEX IQ prosthetic knee brace and how its mechanical design allows the knee to bend. The brace uses rigid plastic beams and connectors arranged to form curved supports around the upper and lower leg. Short axles on both sides act as pivot points, allowing the two sections to swivel as the knee bends. This project focuses on mechanical design and creating a supportive structure without motors or electronics.

